{"id": "EUVD-2026-97580", "enisaUuid": "2ca721d9-85ca-342b-b199-1a3b7d62a2be", "description": "ImageMagick before 6.9.13-57 and 7.x before 7.1.2-32 contains a memory leak in the wavelet-denoise operation, which fails to release allocated memory when a required resource cannot be acquired. Attackers can repeatedly trigger wavelet-denoise processing under resource-constrained conditions to leak memory and degrade service availability.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T15:36:33", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-9f9w-84g3-vp2c", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/15892fc0dc050a3693e28a214478a8d8488d648c", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/0d2544e641848462e8b469c06cde69d7d77c35c6", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-before-6.9.13-57-and-7-x-before-7.1.2-32-memory-leak-in-wavelet-denoise-operation"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109278", "GHSA-rm64-w8m2-8frm"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "343507b4-1fc9-37ce-b536-b4007270d0c4", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.9.13-57"}, {"id": "484214c2-c377-373b-8ef2-e69ea3ec753b", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0-0 <7.1.2-32"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2d69066d-9073-3542-b489-7b94a3e81ab1", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}